<title>USA: First Citizens Q1 net, share fall.</title>
<headline>First Citizens Q1 net, share fall.</headline>
<dateline>RALEIGH, N.C. 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three Months Ended March 31</p>
<p> (thousands, except share data)	   1997		 1996</p>
<p> Interest income			   $136,439	  $129,568</p>
<p> Interest expense			    61,706	    62,424</p>
<p> Net interest income			 74,733	    67,144</p>
<p> Provision for loan losses		  1,567	     1,544</p>
<p>Net interest income after provision</p>
<p>  for loan losses			    73,166	    65,600</p>
<p> Noninterest income			  23,414	    23,885</p>
<p> Noninterest expense			 70,584	    63,285</p>
<p> Income before income taxes		25,996	    26,200</p>
<p> Income taxes				   9,404	     9,374</p>
<p> Net income				    16,592	    16,826</p>
<p> Net income per share			  1.46		1.52</p>
<p> Cash dividends per share		    0.25	     0.225</p>
<p>Profitability Information (annualized)</p>
<p> Return on average assets		   0.85%	     0.91%</p>
<p> Return on average equity		   10.85	     12.40</p>
<p>Taxable-equivalent net yield on</p>
<p>  interest-earning assets		    4.24		4.02</p>
<p>NOTES: Net interest income was $74.7 million for Q1 1997, an 11.3 percent increase over Q1 1996. Total deposits as of March 31, 1997 were $6.9 billion, compared to $6.7 billion at March 31, 1996.</p>
<p>Full company name First Citizens Bancshares Inc.</p>
